Position Summary
Soil Values is currently seeking passionate individuals to join its team in Nigeria, as the program continues to expand its impact and work towards creating positive changes in agriculture and sustainable soil management. In view of this and to effectively carry out technical activities of the program, there is a need to recruit a short term consultant as a technical officer to provide short-term technical support on soil fertility management activities within the Soil Values Program, contributing to the implementation, monitoring, and reporting of technical activities with focus on Integrated Soil Fertility Management (ISFM), soil health diagnostics, and farmer capacity building.
Responsibilities
The short term consultant will be responsible for delivering capacity-building programs and resources to ensure the successful implementation and sustainability of the intervention areas of the Soil Values Program at the country level. He / She will also be responsible for co-designing and implementing agricultural extension programs to support small holder producers in adopting bundled improved practices and technologies. This role involves close collaboration with local communities, government agencies, and other stakeholders to enhance productivity and sustainability. Other responsibilities include but not limited to the following:
Capacity Building and Community Engagement
Conduct workshops, seminars, and field demonstrations to train extension agents and farmers on bundled ISFM technologies to improve Soil health;
Support identified national partners in conducting training on identified bundled ISFM & SWC technologies;
Coordinate with local implementing partners, extension agents, and agro-input suppliers;
Foster a collaborative learning environment among extension teams;
Engage with local communities to understand their needs and challenges;
Build trust and strong relationships with farmers and community leaders;
Encourage community participation and feedback in extension programs.
Technical Support
Contribute to the establishment and monitoring of demonstration plots in target communities;
Offer on-site advice and support to farmers on issues such as pest control, integrated soil fertility management, soil and water conservation practices, crop selection, and irrigation practices;
Promote the adoption of innovative and sustainable soil health management practices;
Document field observations, success stories, and technical learning from field activities;
Provide technical support to the MELS Coordinator by assisting in the review and collation of farmers database and farmer profiling;
Any other duties assigned to the success of the project.
Implementation and Coordination
Coordinate the delivery of extension services, including training, demonstrations, and field visits;
Document field observations, success stories, and technical learning from field activities and advisory tools for digital dissemination of extension messages;
Support the development of technical briefs, training materials, and field reports;
Work with local extension agents and community-based organizations to reach target beneficiaries;
Ensure timely and effective implementation of extension activities;
Participate in regular team meetings and provide technical updates as required.
Requirements
To be eligible to apply, candidate must have the following qualifications:
Bachelor’s degree in agriculture, Agricultural Extension, Agronomy, crop science or a related field;
Strong knowledge of agricultural practices, crop management, and sustainable farming techniques;
Excellent in communication, technical writing, interpersonal, and organizational skills;
Ability to work independently and as part of a team;
Proficiency in using computer applications and digital tools for communication / data analysis and be comfortable in presentations;
Willingness to travel extensively within the assigned region;
Fluency in Hausa Language will be an added advantage.

Education
A good first degree in Accounting, Finance or any related discipline;
A Master’s degree in Finance, Business Management.
Professional Requirements
A professional qualification in accounting such as ACA/ACCA;
Any of the following additional qualifications will be an added advantage:
Certified Internal Auditor
Certified Information Systems Auditor (CISA)
Certified Fraud Examination
Registration with the Financial Reporting Council
Experience
Not less than 10 years post qualification experience, 8 years of which should be as an Internal Auditor and at least 5 years in a senior position;
Experience in risk-based auditing methodology;
Advanced computer skills on MS Office tools and accounting software;
Strong data analytical skills;
Proven Knowledge of internal auditing standards and procedures, laws, rules and regulations;
High attention to detail and excellent analytical skills;
Experience in managing a team and dealing with clients;
Experience in a Financial services, Telecoms, ICT, Energy, and/or Fintech company.

Job Summary
Tetra Pak is a global leader in packaging and processing solutions for the food industry. Our mission is to ensure food is safe and available everywhere, and we achieve this through innovation, sustainability, and digital transformation.
Within our Processing Solutions and Equipment (PSE) unit, we are accelerating the integration of artificial intelligence (AI) and machine learning (ML) to drive smarter, more predictive, and efficient operations.
The Strategy and Operational Insights team, part of Strategy & Operational Excellence (S&OE), plays a key role in this transformation.
We are looking for an Operational Insights Driver who is passionate about leveraging AI and advanced analytics to unlock new opportunities, optimize workflows, and enhance decision-making across our Capital Equipment Projects (CEP) organization.
In this role, you will be at the forefront of developing AI-powered solutions, automating processes, and delivering predictive insights that shape the future of industrial food processing.
You will collaborate with global teams to design and implement data-driven strategies that align with our business goals and push the boundaries of what’s possible with emerging technologies.
If you are excited about applying AI to real-world challenges and want to be part of a global team driving digital innovation, this is your opportunity.
This position can be based at any of our offices or sites worldwide, and extensive travel is not required.
Candidates must be available to work in a hybrid model of three days in the office and two days from home.Tetra Pak is not sponsoring visa or relocation for this position.
What you will do
As an Operational Insights Driver, you will:
Play a pivotal role in enhancing our strategic capabilities through technology, data science and analysis;
Design, develop, and maintain dashboards and actionable insights into business performance;
Explore and implement AI techniques to enhance data analysis;
Collaborate with cross-functional teams to identify data requirements and ensure alignment with business goals and strategic priorities;
Analyze operational data to identify performance trends, bottlenecks, and opportunities for improvement across operations;
Continuously explore and integrate AI technologies to improve reporting, forecasting, and data-driven decision-making;
Ensure the accuracy, consistency, and relevance of data used in insights and reports;
Drive continuous improvement of data reporting processes to support operational and strategic decisions;
Explore and implement AI technologies across various operational functions to optimize performance and drive value creation;
Seek for improvement areas and being accountable for the feasibility analysis and solution development, fostering innovation and maintaining high-quality standards for insights delivery;
Participate on global Business Transformation Projects connected to CE operation.
Requirements
We believe you have:
Bachelor’s Degree in Data Science, Data Management, Information Science, or a related field; a master’s degree in business, management, or a related field is a plus;
Experience in high-tech growth environments, with digital solutions such as RPA development, Power Platform (SharePoint lists, Power Automate, and Power Apps), and AI systems;
Familiarity with process automation, AI techniques, and tools like Power BI for creating dashboards and visualizing data;
Experience with other business analytics tools, coding experience (Python), basic DBA (database administration), and SQL Server knowledge are a plus;
Strong understanding of AI/ML concepts, including supervised and unsupervised learning, predictive modeling, and natural language processing;
Experience applying machine learning algorithms to real-world business problems, preferably in operations, forecasting, or process optimization;
Familiarity with AI platforms and frameworks such as TensorFlow, PyTorch, or Azure Machine Learning is a plus;
Ability to translate business challenges into AI-driven solutions and communicate complex technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders;
Strong analytical skills and mindset, crucial for analyzing data, identifying trends, and making data-driven decisions;
Agility, strong drive for results, ability to deliver on time and under challenging situations, effective communication skills, and proficiency in stakeholder and change management;
Proficiency in English.
We Offer You
A variety of exciting challenges with ample opportunities for development and training in a truly global landscape
A culture that pioneers a spirit of innovation where our industry experts drive visible results
An equal opportunity employment experience that values diversity and inclusion
Market competitive compensation and benefits with flexible working arrangements

Position Summary
Ponticelli Freres, an international industrial group serving companies in the oil and gas sector, is recruiting for its entity Ponticelli Nigeria for a subsea project.
Would you like to develop your experience as Subsea Project Manager (M/F) and help transform the world as part of a family-owned group that strives to provide people with what they will always need: energy, health, water, food and safety, while sincerely respecting the planet and its employees.
We are offering you the opportunity to join us in a technical support contract. The position is based in Port-Harcourt in Nigeria.
As the appointed representative of the Ponticelli Frères Group Management on a dedicated subsea project, the Subsea Project Manager is responsible for overseeing all aspects of execution, ensuring the successful delivery of projects focused on subsea mudmats and structural components.
He/she guarantees:
Full compliance with Quality, Safety, Health, and Environmental (QSSE) policies throughout the project lifecycle.
Fulfillment of all contractual obligations towards clients, service providers, and subcontractors.
Achievement of the financial and performance goals set by the Ponticelli Group.
Effective communication and coordination with external stakeholders.
The Subsea Project Manager is fully dedicated to a single project and plays a key role in both strategic oversight and day-to-day management.
The position we are offering involves the following main tasks :
ensure compliance with the Group’s Quality, Safety, Health, and Environment (QSSE) policies throughout the project;
prepare, review, and validate project offers and contracts with management;
monitor project budgets and control expenses to ensure profitability;
analyze project progress and profitability; implement corrective actions if needed;
communicate technical and schedule deviations to the client proactively;
manage invoicing, variations, and additional work submissions with clients;
organize and lead project kickoff and regular progress meetings (internal and with client);
supervise project execution, ensuring alignment with safety, quality, cost, and schedule targets;
coordinate resource allocation including personnel, equipment, subcontractors, and purchases;
manage subcontractor selection, work oversight, and performance evaluation;
ensure all technical and administrative documentation is accurate and compliant;
handle project closure activities including punch list resolution and final acceptance;
conduct project debriefs and report feedback to management; Manage and support the project team, including performance reviews and training needs;
participate in recruitment, team management, and company representation with third parties.
Profile Wanted
You have a engineering degree (general or specialized in subsea, structural, or mechanical disciplines) or equivalent field/project experience in offshore/subsea construction and stuctures. Also, you have at least 8 years of experience on subsea projects.
You have a deep understanding of subsea engineering, particularly related to mudmats and subsea metallic structures.
You have proven expertise in project and business management. You have the ability to implement and enforce QSSE policy.
You are recognised for your strong delegation and supervision capabilities.
You have experience in managing complex subsea projects from tender to completion. You are capable of leading multi-disciplinary project teams.
You have developped skilled in stakeholder management and client communication.
You are autonomous, proactive, reliable and rigorous. Also highly organized and detail-oriented. You have a strong interpersonal and communication skills.
You are available and willing to travel or work offshore if required.
You are proficient in using IT tools for project tracking and reporting.
You have the ability to define and use project performance indicators (KPIs).
You are fluent in English.
If you would like to join us in supporting global change, we look forward to hearing from you!
